  "case_id": "02_mia_sakura_selected_cast",
  "composer": {
    "accepted_prose": "Ted turns to Mia first, his expression open but unreadable. Mia glances down, a faint smile touching her lips as she tucks a strand of hair behind her ear.\n\n\"It was… nice,\" she says, her voice soft. \"You were very considerate. I think a quieter evening is good for getting used to a new place.\"\n\nShe meets his eyes for a moment, then looks away, her cheeks faintly pink. She does not mention the way her heart had quickened when he laughed, or the small, foolish hope that had lodged itself beneath her ribs.\n\nSakura watches from the armchair, her posture upright, hands folded in her lap. She waits until Mia finishes, then speaks with measured precision.\n\n\"I found your conduct appropriate,\" she says. \"You did not impose. I will reserve any fuller judgment until I have observed more.\"\n\nHer grey eyes hold his without warmth or hostility. She gives a slight, professional nod, then falls silent.",
